{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Who is…</b> This verse is a witness to the uprightness of my interpretation." "<b>My servant…</b> The meaning: you are blind, for you say that there is no blind one except the prophet." "<b>As a messenger I send.</b> He is the emissary of HaShem, and likewise it is written, 'And Haggai said, the messenger of YHWH' (Haggai 1:13)." "<b>Who is blind like the one made whole.</b> Like 'and he who regards a command, he is whole' (Proverbs 13:13) from the root שלם, and likewise the meshulam is the righteous one." "<b>And blind like the servant of YHWH.</b> Who serves HaShem, even if he is not a prophet."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {1 "Resolved the bracketed [אין] supplied in the Hebrew text."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:37.711726958Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}